Campaign session-workspace, over Private/UI/FlowVizWorkspaceModel.cpp with
filter FlowViz.UI.WorkspaceModel. Run 2026-08-06 12:55-13:14Z in
wind-worktrees/dispatchobs against ef0c4ad, 10 arms.

    verdict   arm
    --------  ----------------------------------------------------------
    killed    the session's field id dropped -- opens the first non-mask field
    killed    the apply runs BEFORE the case opens (the ordering hazard)
    killed    a missing case ABORTS -- the panels never arrive
    INVALID   a missing case is opened ANYWAY            <-- see BELOW
    killed    the transfer function is not captured (SaveSession null)
    killed    the clip model is not captured
    killed    the slice model is not captured
    killed    the probe model is not captured
    killed    the player is not captured
    SURVIVED  IDENTITY CONTROL                                    (correct)

    killed 8  SURVIVED 1  INVALID 1  UNSCORED 0  skipped 0

The identity control SURVIVED, which is what makes the other nine verdicts
readable at all: the harness was demonstrably able to let a no-op through, so
the eight kills are about the mutants rather than about a standing red. Its
per-arm log (the last one written, see the caveat below) shows all four tests
Success. Baseline built clean and the suite was green before any arm was
applied.

THE INVALID IS A REAL FINDING ABOUT THE ARM, NOT ABOUT THE CODE.

    if (State.bCaseFound)  ->  if (true)

    FlowVizWorkspaceModel.cpp:386:10: error: code will never be executed
    [-Werror,-Wunreachable-code]

`if (true)` lets the compiler prove the else branch dead, and this module builds
with -Werror. The BEHAVIOUR the arm wanted to express - open the case even when
the parse said it is missing, so CloseCase runs and the user loses the case they
had open - is a real defect worth scoring; the arm was only wrong about how to
express it invisibly to the compiler. Re-run as session-workspace-arm4.txt with

    if (State.bCaseFound)  ->  if (!State.ResolvedCasePath.IsEmpty())

which is true in exactly the cases `if (true)` would be (the enclosing guard has
already established the path is non-empty) while leaving the else formally
reachable. Repo memory unreachable-code-cannot-be-differentially-tested.

Until that re-run lands, ONE BRANCH OF THIS FUNCTION IS UNVERIFIED BY MUTATION:
nothing has yet demonstrated that the `bCaseFound` test is load-bearing. It is
asserted by FlowViz.UI.WorkspaceModel.SessionMissingCase - which checks that a
load whose case moved reports FileNotFound and leaves the previously-open case
open - but an assertion existing is not the same as an assertion being able to
fail, which is the entire reason this campaign exists.

WHICH ASSERTIONS KILLED WHICH ARM. DERIVED, NOT READ OFF A LOG - and that is a
defect in how this campaign was run rather than a property of the results.
TEST_LOG was pointed at a single path that mutate.sh OVERWRITES per arm, so only
the last arm's log (the identity control) survived to be read. The attribution
below is reasoned from which assertions each mutant necessarily breaks, and is
weaker evidence than the clip-seam READMEs beside it, which quote real failure
text. A future campaign should point TEST_LOG at a per-arm path.

    field id dropped        SessionRoundTrip and SessionMissingCase both assert
                            Player.GetFieldId() and TransferFunction.GetFieldId()
                            equal the fixture's field. NAME_None opens the first
                            non-mask field instead, so both go red.

    apply before open       SessionRoundTrip. OpenCase resets playback settings,
                            seeks to frame 0 and resets the crop box, so an apply
                            that ran first is silently undone: the restored
                            playback settings, physical time and crop assertions
                            fail while the case itself still opens.

    missing case ABORTS     SessionMissingCase, and ONLY that test - this is the
                            arm the new test was written for. Its whole subject
                            is VerifyRestoredPanels running with the case half
                            deliberately absent. Under this mutant the early
                            return skips ApplyToViewModels entirely, so every
                            panel assertion fails. SessionRoundTrip cannot see
                            it: its case is found, so FirstFailure is Ok and the
                            inserted guard never fires.

    five null-capture arms  SessionRoundTrip. Each drops one view model from the
                            capture, so that model's values come back as
                            defaults after the reload. They are five separate
                            arms rather than one compound arm on purpose: a
                            compound arm dies on whichever model is checked
                            first and the other four ride along untested. Repo
                            memory a-compound-mutant-scores-like-a-narrow-one.

WHAT THE CAMPAIGN DID NOT COVER. Every arm here is about the MODEL. Nothing in
this file's tests binds a UCFDVizVolumeComponent, so no arm could have shown
that a restored session reaches the renderer - the panels can be perfectly
restored while the image on screen is still the previous session's. That gap is
task #64 and is covered by FlowViz.UI.Workspace.SessionSeam, in a different
file, against a different filter.
